{
  "$comment": "S21 · PR 414 (Blueprint B7.3) — the saved browser journeys, replayed by tools/journeys.mjs on the owner's schedule (Reports › Site health; infra/deploy/journeys.sh) on a phone and a desktop screen. Plain Playwright, AI not needed. Each journey is a list of steps: `open` a path (signed out for the customer, as the read-only check account for the others) and `expect` a selector there; `follow` the first link matching a selector (the products and categories are the owner's, so none is named here; with `optional`, a shop with none skips the rest of that journey and says so); `click` the first enabled element matching a selector; `api` sends a request from the page and expects a status (the permission limits: each write here is harmless even if it were allowed, an invalid body, and must be refused with 403). The staff journeys sign in as the read-only check account (like the smoke test), so they walk what each role opens and prove a write is refused; a role's own account per journey is a follow-up. A step fails on a 5xx, the error screen, a console error, a page error, a failed request, or a missing `expect`. The customer journey never adds to the bag (that would hold real stock) and never places an order (a real order on the live shop); the order, invoice and tracking pages are opened with no order (their 'not found' cards). `expectAny`: any one of the selectors. PR 416: `touch` opens a screen as a phone (its viewport tag, touch taps), where the UI checks also measure tap sizes and form text (the device gate's touch rules); the UI checks run after every step that opens or changes a page when the owner switched them on (Reports › Site health, `health.uiChecks`). PR 421 (B6.6): the auditor's sandbox refuses every write from the check account's session before any permission is checked, its own two-step route too; the last accountant step proves it on the live site. PR 414 follow-up (CN-013 go-live gate, phase 2): the journeys with `group` run only when that group is asked for (JOURNEYS_GROUP; journeys.yml's `group` input), never in the owner's schedule. The `go-live-gate` group walks every live check of the simulation findings (docs/qa/SIMULATION-REPORT.md, SIM-F-…) that a signed-out visitor or the read-only check account can see, each step naming its findings (`sim`); it orders nothing, adds nothing to the bag and changes no setting. A feature behind one of the owner's switches is checked as it is set: `switches` (on: the selector is there; off: it is not), `when` / `unless` (the step runs only with the switches all on / all off), read once a run from GET /api/admin/settings as the check account. `expect` as a list: each selector; `expectNone`: none of them; an `open` with `status`: that answer (404 for a page a switch closes).",
